/T (Three management questions answered are: Which line has the highest defect rate? Which machinesexceed the fleet-wide mean? Is the night shift associated with higher defect rates than the day shift?The first question is especially sensitive to join coverage. Line C is 4.07% when all production recordsarekept, but only 2.55% when M13 records are silently dropped by an inner join. The difference is 1.523percentage points. Excluding unmatched M13 disproportionately removes high-defect records and understatesthe line- C quality problem; this is a concrete reliability risk shown by the experiment, not merelyatheoretical concern. )
