/T (The chosen limitation is expensive per-row computation and avoidable object-string storage in the Q6 weekly reporting workflow. On the same 100,000 records, apply required 1846.6 ms against only 0.733 ms for column vectorisation. The full DataFrame consumed 18.702 MB. The principal cause is row-wise Python overhead and repetitive object-string metadata, not an inappropriate grouping rule or data leakage. This is a computation and representation bottleneck observed with the existing inputs. )
