2021 0 obj
<<
/Title (The four-machine readings and seven-row production example are transcribed directly from the assignment. Where the assignment requires larger datasets, they are generated reproducibly using fixed NumPy seeds: Q1 = 20260501, Q2 = 20260502, Q3 = 20260503, and Q4 machine metadata = 20260504. The large production input contains 1,000 distinct records plus 12 duplicate rows deliberately included to test cleaning, leaving precisely 1,000 cleaned records. Missing values and unmatched machine metadata are intentionally included to test quality controls. Generated data are experimental records rather than observations claimed to have come from a real factory.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1798 0 R
/Next 2022 0 R
>>
endobj
2022 0 obj
<<
/Title (Every displayed measurement was computed by executing the matching Python source file. Raw execution logs are under Outputs/, and detailed machine/day statistics, merge records, grouping results, and benchmark measurements are saved as separate CSV or JSON files. Timings are wall-clock measurements in this execution environment and can vary by hardware and system load.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1798 0 R
/Prev 2021 0 R
>>
